+
+#### [whisper.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp)
+> **Description:** whisper.cpp ports Whisper to high-performance C and C++ with a focus on local inference, quantization, hardware efficiency, and minimal runtime dependencies. That makes it attractive for podcasters who want offline transcripts on laptops, desktops, or edge devices without a large Python stack. The README highlights support for Apple Silicon, CPU-only inference, GPU acceleration paths, and lightweight distribution, which is useful for building desktop tools or command-line episode workflows. GitHub showed `42k` stars, C++ as the primary language, and an MIT license. Activity remained healthy in 2026.
+
