+#### [whisper-timestamped](https://github.com/linto-ai/whisper-timestamped)
+> **Description:** whisper-timestamped adds word-level timestamps and confidence estimates to Whisper output and is explicit about improving timing quality beyond the default one-second segment granularity. For podcasters, that means easier speaker quote clipping, more accurate subtitles, and better alignment when turning transcripts into chapter markers or social clips. The README explains how it augments Whisper outputs rather than replacing the core models, so it fits well as a post-processing layer in a production pipeline. GitHub showed about `3.3k` stars, Python as the primary language, and an AGPL-3.0 license. The latest visible commit was on October 30, 2024.
