+### Gaps Worth Noting
+
+Podcast-native open source AI apps are still much rarer than the surrounding speech and audio infrastructure. The strongest GitHub ecosystem today is still in these adjacent layers:
+
+- Speech recognition and timestamping
+- Speaker diarization and VAD
+- Noise suppression and source separation
+- TTS and voice cloning
+
+If you specifically want open source repos that look like polished "Descript alternatives for podcasters," that category still has fewer than five mature, widely used GitHub projects. That gap is real.
+
+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for podcasters in 2026?
+For most podcasters, the practical stack is `Whisper` or `faster-whisper` for transcription, `pyannote-audio` for diarization, `silero-vad` for speech segmentation, and `DeepFilterNet` or `Demucs` for cleanup. If you also need synthetic narration, `coqui-ai/TTS` and `OpenVoice` are the strongest GitHub-first choices in this list.
+
+### Which GitHub repos are best for podcast transcription with speaker labels?
+Use `WhisperX` or `Whisper` for transcripts, then pair them with `pyannote-audio` for diarization. That combination is one of the most common open source ways to produce speaker-aware transcripts for interviews and roundtables.
+
+### Are there free AI tools for podcasters that work fully offline?
+Yes. `whisper.cpp`, `Handy`, `Whisper`, `faster-whisper`, and `silero-vad` can all support local-first workflows. Exact hardware requirements vary, but you can build a fully offline pipeline on a modern desktop or laptop.
+
+### What open source AI tools help clean bad podcast audio?
+`DeepFilterNet` is a strong denoising pick, `resemble-enhance` is useful for speech restoration, and `Demucs` helps when speech is tangled up with music or other mixed content. In practice, podcasters often combine at least two of these tools.
+
+### Which AI GitHub repos are useful for podcast show notes and quote extraction?
+Start with `whisper-timestamped` or `WhisperX` so the transcript has usable timing, then use `transcript-seeker` or your own search layer to mine quotes and recurring themes. Timestamp quality matters more than model size for this use case.
+
+### Are there open source alternatives to proprietary podcast AI editors?
+Partially. The ecosystem is strongest in infrastructure repos, not polished all-in-one editors. That means you can build a powerful stack from GitHub projects, but the number of mature OSS repos that feel like complete podcast editing products is still limited.
+
